course: dictionary
lesson: 12417
title: Daredevil and daring words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A daredevil is a person who does dangerous, exciting things, often to show off or to entertain people. «The daredevil walked along a tightrope high above the crowd.» The clues are tightrope, high above and crowd. Walking that high is risky, so a daredevil must be someone who takes big risks on purpose.
explain: Daredevil can also be an adjective, a word that describes a noun. «The crowd gasped at her daredevil jump over the bus.» The jump is bold and risky, so daredevil describes it. Check by swapping in another word: «her risky jump» still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
explain: Look for clues in the words around the unknown word. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Stunts in films and circus shows are done by trained people wearing safety gear. Never copy a stunt at home or from an online «challenge», because a daredevil trick can cause serious harm.
fact: A daredevil is a noun: a person who does dangerous, exciting things.
fact: Daredevil is also an adjective: it describes a risky, bold action, such as a daredevil jump.
fact: Daredevils in films, circuses and stunt shows walk tightropes, jump motorbikes over buses or do wild skateboard tricks.
fact: Real stunts are done by trained people with safety gear, such as helmets and harnesses.
fact: Plural of the noun: daredevils.
exercise: «The daredevil walked along a tightrope high above the crowd.» What is a daredevil? | A person who teaches swimming | A person who sings loudly in a band | A person who sells tickets at a circus | *A person who does dangerous, exciting things
exercise: Find and copy the adjective that describes the jump: «The crowd gasped at her daredevil jump over the bus.» | crowd | gasped | *daredevil | bus
exercise: Why do trained stunt people wear safety gear? | To make their jumps go higher | To keep their hands warm | To look like superheroes in photos | *To stay safe while doing dangerous tricks
test: «Mia tried a daredevil skateboard trick down the steep hill, without a helmet.» What should we think about Mia's trick? | It was a kind present for a friend | *It was risky, and we should not copy it | It was a quiet nap in the sun | It was a slow, safe walk to the shop
test: In «a daredevil jump», what kind of word is daredevil? | *An adjective describing the jump | An adverb telling how the jump was done | A noun naming a person | A verb showing an action
exam: Which sentence describes a daredevil? | Someone who is very tired after school | *Someone who does brave, dangerous, exciting things | Someone who always stays indoors with a book | Someone who cooks dinner for the family
